{"title":"2008 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249aa48167a0ec4808fb235a2796eaffab883dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCE$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cdc4517b7ed61911044dd6122d4f99dcbc817ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF=2FE$\" width=\"89\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/b/86bf31381ea2f4a7c94d8571191b3c9e17c337a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=2DE$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />. What is the ratio of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db8b31c18cec01817c2a504c27bd65c627c7159.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BFD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> to the area of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249aa48167a0ec4808fb235a2796eaffab883dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCE$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cd0313c1b06e23b6ae03cfe53c292b0ac2371db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size((100)); draw((0,0)--(9,0)--(9,9)--(0,9)--cycle); draw((3,0)--(9,9)--(0,3)--cycle); dot((3,0)); dot((0,3)); dot((9,9)); dot((0,0)); dot((9,0)); dot((0,9)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,9), NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (9,9), NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (9,0), SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, (3,0), S); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, (0,0), SW); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, (0,3), W); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"165\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/a/80ab237d874219c53eb155fad5993397982fa98e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{6}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{2}{9}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{5}{18}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{7}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"385\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db8b31c18cec01817c2a504c27bd65c627c7159.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BFD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is the area of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249aa48167a0ec4808fb235a2796eaffab883dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCE$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> subtracted by the the area of the three triangles around it. Arbitrarily assign the side length of the square to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e70951e5f1b40046a0a06bfca96b4332908164d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size((100)); pair A=(0,9), B=(9,9), C=(9,0), D=(3,0), E=(0,0), F=(0,3); pair[] ps={A,B,C,D,E,F}; dot(ps); draw(A--B--C--E--cycle); draw(B--F--D--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A, NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B, NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C, SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D, S); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E, SW); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F, W); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,A--B,N); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,(10,4.5),E); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,D--C,S); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,E--D,S); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,E--F,W); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,F--A,W); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"165\" />\n</p><p>The ratio of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db8b31c18cec01817c2a504c27bd65c627c7159.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BFD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> to the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249aa48167a0ec4808fb235a2796eaffab883dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCE$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/8/9c8ba1a5d01139d2d5b5a9f885680737cb9d92f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{36-12-12-2}{36} = \\frac{10}{36} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{5}{18}}\\]\" width=\"271\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a0789bd57f33e9ba6593c23331278e1f022b7739.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{FE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and that from there we can infer that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/d/93d638251918cca1b062e637431acf7fb004574e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AF} = 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />. We also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/0/2c074cb070955e2110464fdbe835ce7425a927fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{ED} = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/3/363be9902cbce055f36ed2289df41b432c671144.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DC} = 2x$\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />. The area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7a8dfd3e68089fff4bb33022c7eb7d21b74a2ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BFD$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is the square's area subtracted from the area of the excess triangles, which is simply these equations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/262a918d2b8868d31440e652818dcbbfb7ea701d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9x^2 - (3x^2 + \\dfrac{x}{2}^2 + 3x^2)\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"36\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03b44fc847cc25af310f7f63f90daa4c65ca5ba2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9x^2 - 6.5x^2\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d3b42b8dec68251d0f5badc63a93e797a542887.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2.5x^2\\]\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" />\nThus, the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7a9304647a704b4bf81dbb2ef5401be054db4ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.5x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />. We can now put the ratio of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7a8dfd3e68089fff4bb33022c7eb7d21b74a2ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BFD$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />'s area to the area of the square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249aa48167a0ec4808fb235a2796eaffab883dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCE$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> as a fraction. We have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/d/73d42618922762eb9c32312853fbf75294bdfbef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{2.5x^2}{9x^2}\\]\" width=\"41\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb2f63597477e6cf0a582e3dff84f4921bd2a4da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{2.5\\cancel{x^2}}{9\\cancel{x^2}}\\]\" width=\"43\" height=\"42\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/c/f6c04ae3a3bf02739a3ac1a594dd2c4603cbeacf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{2.5}{9}\\]\" width=\"23\" height=\"38\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c7b60b19d82c2f43f09ba0836a039de0ce8a015.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{5}{18}\\]\" width=\"18\" height=\"38\" />\nThus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0d6c2eb56c9cac0db52d455cdefd20c7eaa7371.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{5}{18}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"69\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~Mr.BigBrain_AoPS\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/abSgjn4Qs34?t=528\">https://youtu.be/abSgjn4Qs34?t=528</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8\" title=\"2008 AMC 8\">2008 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2008\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2008 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2008 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" ti